 # Preview Specifications
 
+## Preview Retrieval and Caching
+
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-001**: When a request identifies an unknown clip revision, the system SHALL return 404 without enqueuing a render job.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-002**: When the requested preview is cached, the system SHALL return 200 with the JPEG for the requested revision and renderer version.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-003**: When concurrent requests miss the cache for the same preview key, the system SHALL return 202 with the same job ticket and a two-second retry interval while one shared render job is pending.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-004**: When admitting a completed preview would exceed 12 GiB of cached JPEG data, the system SHALL evict entries before admission so the cache remains within that limit.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-005**: When a render job fails, the system SHALL release its deduplication entry so a later request can enqueue a new job.
+
+## 2Q Queue Management
+
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-010**: The system SHALL maintain two LRU queues: Inqueue (target 30% of cache) for entries accessed zero or one time, and Outqueue (target 70% of cache) for entries accessed two or more times.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-011**: When a new preview completes rendering, the system SHALL add it to Inqueue, advancing the tail.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-012**: When a cached preview in Inqueue is accessed for the second time, the system SHALL move that entry to the tail of Outqueue and remove it from Inqueue.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-013**: When a cached preview in Outqueue is accessed, the system SHALL refresh it in place, moving the entry to the tail of Outqueue.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-014**: When admission would exceed 12 GiB total cache, the system SHALL evict LRU entries from Inqueue until Inqueue occupies no more than 30% of the 12 GiB budget (approximately 3.6 GiB).
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-015**: If Inqueue reaches its target size per PREVIEW-014 but total cache still exceeds 12 GiB, the system SHALL evict LRU entries from Outqueue until cache size returns within budget.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-016**: Evicted entries SHALL be removed from both the queue and the disk cache.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-017**: The 30% / 70% queue size target split is approximate and MAY drift within a session as entries are accessed and evicted; the split requires no active rebalancing.
